WEBVTT

00:10.400 --> 00:13.040
We're truly grateful that 
all of you could join us

00:13.040 --> 00:17.240
to celebrate the start of 
our new life together today.

00:17.240 --> 00:20.750
I'm sure the two of us still have 
much to learn and experience,

00:20.750 --> 00:24.710
so please continue to give us 
guidance and encouragement.

00:24.710 --> 00:26.580
They look so happy.

00:26.580 --> 00:28.040
Yes, they really do.

00:28.040 --> 00:29.750
Oh, Touya—

00:29.750 --> 00:32.940
Oops, it's Your Royal Highness now.

00:32.940 --> 00:37.040
Your Royal Highness, I'm truly grateful 
you could spare some words

00:37.040 --> 00:38.720
to congratulate these two today.

00:38.720 --> 00:43.310
General Leon, Olba-san, 
once again, congratulations.

00:45.990 --> 00:49.710
Thinking about it now, this 
might never have happened

00:49.710 --> 00:51.930
if you hadn't bridged the gap between them.

00:51.930 --> 00:53.080
That's true.

00:53.080 --> 00:57.760
The Strand family is truly blessed to 
have forged such a good connection.

00:57.760 --> 00:59.120
Father!

00:59.120 --> 01:00.700
Over here!

01:00.700 --> 01:02.870
Well, please excuse me.

01:02.870 --> 01:05.040
I'll see you later, Your Royal Highness.

01:05.770 --> 01:07.900
They both seemed so happy.

01:07.900 --> 01:12.040
Of course they'd be happy 
at their children's wedding.

01:13.710 --> 01:14.820
Touya!

01:14.820 --> 01:17.710
When we will have our wedding ceremony?

01:17.710 --> 01:18.570
Huh?!

01:18.570 --> 01:21.680
I'm ready to marry into the 
Brunhild family at any time!

01:21.680 --> 01:24.690
Shh! Not so loud!

01:24.690 --> 01:27.650
We haven't formally announced that yet!

01:27.980 --> 01:30.890
Seeing such a lovely 
wedding ceremony really does

01:30.890 --> 01:33.360
make one think about when 
their own time will come.

01:33.730 --> 01:35.060
Our...

01:35.060 --> 01:36.570
...wedding ceremonies...

01:41.530 --> 01:44.830
Right. I'll have to have six 
wedding ceremonies, won't I?

01:44.830 --> 01:46.850
Assuming six is all you have...

01:46.850 --> 01:48.000
Huh?!

01:48.000 --> 01:51.000
Please spare me from having any more!

01:51.820 --> 01:55.900
Gather up your tears

01:55.900 --> 01:58.300
And release your unhindered light

01:58.300 --> 02:03.230
That shines like a diamond

02:03.230 --> 02:04.740
Don't worry, don't care

02:04.740 --> 02:07.780
Follow your heart

02:18.570 --> 02:24.830
Every time I spoke of my
dreams, they felt closed off

02:24.830 --> 02:31.140
Even that bird and that sky
seemed monochrome to me

02:31.140 --> 02:37.590
Yet you were there in my path,
your eyes brimming with strength

02:37.590 --> 02:44.270
Time then stopped, and deep within
my heart something began to stir

02:46.340 --> 02:50.350
Don't be afraid, and run forth

02:50.350 --> 02:52.720
If we only have one life to live

02:52.720 --> 02:59.030
Then be true to yourself,
so you don't regret it

02:59.030 --> 03:03.120
Gather up your tears

03:03.120 --> 03:05.500
And release your unhindered light

03:05.500 --> 03:10.520
That shines like a diamond

03:10.520 --> 03:11.990
Don't worry, don't care

03:11.990 --> 03:15.140
Follow your heart

03:20.970 --> 03:25.970
Episode 9

03:20.970 --> 03:25.970
Day-Off Dates and the Female Knight

03:28.600 --> 03:30.560
Let's cultivate our love!

03:31.590 --> 03:32.520
What?

03:33.980 --> 03:36.680
After seeing that wedding 
ceremony, I had a thought!

03:36.680 --> 03:39.350
We should learn more about each other,

03:39.350 --> 03:40.780
open our hearts to each other,

03:40.780 --> 03:42.700
and cultivate our love!

03:42.700 --> 03:44.040
Uh-huh...

03:44.040 --> 03:46.080
Wonderful idea, Yumina!

03:46.080 --> 03:49.280
I've constantly been thinking the same thing!

03:49.280 --> 03:50.180
Right?

03:50.180 --> 03:50.910
Right!

03:50.910 --> 03:53.370
Um, what do you mean specifically?

03:53.370 --> 03:55.720
Through dates, of course!

03:56.290 --> 03:57.340
Dates?!

03:57.340 --> 04:02.970
You mean where a man and woman engaged 
in courtship go out to places together?!

04:02.970 --> 04:04.070
Yes!

04:04.070 --> 04:05.850
They're meant to strengthen intimacy,

04:05.850 --> 04:10.570
and primarily involve going out to eat, 
shopping, or attending a theater.

04:10.570 --> 04:13.190
Wait, strengthen intimacy?

04:13.190 --> 04:15.650
But I'm already engaged to all of you.

04:15.650 --> 04:19.470
You've been leaving us 
alone too much lately.

04:19.470 --> 04:22.490
Are you the type to not feed 
the fish you've already hooked?

04:22.490 --> 04:23.500
Huh?

04:23.500 --> 04:25.200
I-I was thinking that, too.

04:25.200 --> 04:28.510
Yesterday, I only saw you at meal times.

04:28.510 --> 04:29.940
Me, too. It's...

04:29.940 --> 04:32.790
Well, it's a bit lonely.

04:32.790 --> 04:35.280
<i>I suppose I have been busy 
running around lately,</i>

04:35.280 --> 04:37.500
<i>so I haven't made much time for everyone.</i>

04:37.500 --> 04:38.400
See?

04:38.400 --> 04:43.130
All of us want to spend time with you 
and share memories together.

04:44.950 --> 04:46.290
Memories...

04:46.980 --> 04:48.490
All right.

04:48.490 --> 04:51.220
Then shall we all go out together today?

04:51.220 --> 04:53.000
Y-You mean it?!

04:53.000 --> 04:54.060
Yay!

04:59.480 --> 05:01.280
Sorry for the wait.

05:10.540 --> 05:11.860
Those are...

05:12.370 --> 05:16.170
I had them specially ordered from 
Zanac's shop for a day like this.

05:16.170 --> 05:19.460
The designs came from you.

05:21.920 --> 05:23.630
So...

05:23.630 --> 05:25.080
Um...

05:25.080 --> 05:26.630
H-How are they?

05:27.010 --> 05:27.730
Huh?

05:27.730 --> 05:28.940
Give us your impression.

05:28.940 --> 05:31.000
Oh, yeah, you're all cute.

05:31.000 --> 05:32.560
They suit each one of you well.

05:33.920 --> 05:36.370
Now, off to our date!

05:36.370 --> 05:37.900
Yeah!

05:37.900 --> 05:39.770
But first...

05:42.690 --> 05:44.330
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

05:44.330 --> 05:46.060
And once more!

05:45.470 --> 05:47.700
Uh, what are you doing?

05:46.060 --> 05:47.700
And once more!

05:57.660 --> 05:59.880
What a lovely city!

06:00.220 --> 06:03.210
The breeze feels so nice.

06:03.750 --> 06:05.170
Refreese, huh?

06:05.170 --> 06:08.700
There are all kinds of shops here, 
so it does seem like fun.

06:09.870 --> 06:11.010
Uh...

06:11.010 --> 06:13.630
We'll swap out when our time comes!

06:13.630 --> 06:15.220
What a shame.

06:16.010 --> 06:18.190
Hey, aren't you clinging too close?

06:18.190 --> 06:20.520
<i>So that rock-paper-scissors game...</i>

06:20.520 --> 06:23.470
<i>Now I get it. This is embarrassing.</i>

06:23.470 --> 06:25.530
<i>Though I am happy.</i>

06:34.540 --> 06:36.280
They're cute.

06:36.280 --> 06:37.920
Shall I get some for everyone?

06:37.920 --> 06:39.370
A-Are you sure?

06:41.330 --> 06:43.670
Yeah. To commemorate today.

06:53.430 --> 06:55.680
It's our turn now.

06:57.520 --> 06:59.480
W-Well, shall we eat?

07:00.300 --> 07:02.270
Stop, Touya.

07:02.270 --> 07:03.160
Huh?

07:03.160 --> 07:04.730
Since we're here...

07:06.360 --> 07:07.880
Open wide.

07:07.880 --> 07:09.320
No, uh...

07:09.320 --> 07:11.530
T-Touya! Me, too!

07:12.030 --> 07:13.240
Huh?!

07:13.940 --> 07:15.700
Open wide!

07:22.120 --> 07:24.270
Where shall we go next?

07:25.840 --> 07:28.640
Oh, Touya, look at that.

07:30.130 --> 07:33.620
There's a traveling theater 
troupe in the plaza.

07:33.620 --> 07:36.260
"Buckram the Legendary Dragonslayer," huh?

07:36.260 --> 07:39.480
Doesn't sound like the right 
kind of tale for a date, though.

07:39.480 --> 07:41.320
That's not true.

07:41.320 --> 07:45.570
"Buckram the Legendary Dragonslayer" is a 
tale of romance centered around one woman.

07:45.570 --> 07:47.900
Buckram sets off to 
challenge the dragon so that

07:47.900 --> 07:49.490
he can earn permission 
to wed her, and then—

07:49.490 --> 07:50.680
Stop!

07:50.680 --> 07:53.450
If you spoil the story, it won't be any fun!

07:53.450 --> 07:56.350
S-Sorry, I just...

07:56.350 --> 07:57.750
A romance story, huh?

07:57.750 --> 07:59.640
That should be something we all can enjoy.

07:59.640 --> 08:00.590
Let's go see it.

08:00.590 --> 08:01.300
Yes!

08:01.300 --> 08:02.410
I'm excited!

08:02.410 --> 08:03.950
Hey, dude.

08:03.950 --> 08:05.880
Look at you with all those girls.

08:06.310 --> 08:08.340
Do you need something?

08:08.340 --> 08:11.690
Our wallets have been feeling a little empty,

08:11.690 --> 08:14.690
so we figured you could 
show them some charity.

08:14.690 --> 08:17.640
Or you could share those 
girls with us instead.

08:18.240 --> 08:21.150
Did you think you could 
frighten us by drawing blades?

08:21.150 --> 08:23.240
No chance for me to step in...

08:24.560 --> 08:28.440
I hope rounding them all up and leaving 
them at the knights' station like that

08:28.440 --> 08:30.190
didn't make too much trouble for the knights.

08:30.190 --> 08:31.860
Seemed fine to me.

08:31.860 --> 08:34.280
We'll leave the rest to 
the people of Refreese.

08:34.280 --> 08:37.410
Honestly... Way to ruin our date.

08:37.410 --> 08:39.890
Now, now, the play was interesting,

08:39.890 --> 08:41.530
and we still enjoyed our date.

08:41.530 --> 08:43.120
I know, but...

08:43.120 --> 08:47.460
Besides, I'm really happy I got to 
spend time with you all like this.

08:47.460 --> 08:48.910
Touya...

08:54.170 --> 08:57.380
Hey, don't go making it past tense.

08:57.380 --> 08:59.160
We're going to have more fun after this!

08:59.160 --> 09:01.430
And we'll always be together.

09:01.430 --> 09:02.810
That's right!

09:02.810 --> 09:06.310
Now, let's hurry back to our home.

09:08.110 --> 09:09.250
Hey...

09:17.700 --> 09:20.850
Hey, don't pull me all together!

09:20.850 --> 09:21.580
<i>Yeah...</i>

09:21.580 --> 09:24.740
<i>I want to enjoy these smiles forever.</i>

09:25.490 --> 09:26.580
Is that...

09:36.930 --> 09:40.600
No fair! You left me behind by myself!

09:43.060 --> 09:44.180
Touya!

09:44.180 --> 09:47.010
Today you're spending the 
whole day on a date with me!

09:47.010 --> 09:48.470
Got it?

09:48.470 --> 09:50.020
Yes, yes.

09:51.250 --> 09:53.590
Your Royal Highness! Hello!

09:53.590 --> 09:55.490
Hello to you, too, Princess!

09:55.490 --> 09:57.420
Yes! Hello to you, too!

09:57.420 --> 10:00.450
But it's not "Princess." It's "Grand Duchess"!

10:00.450 --> 10:01.450
Okay!

10:01.450 --> 10:02.650
Sure!

10:02.650 --> 10:04.540
That's not your title yet.

10:04.540 --> 10:07.050
It will be one day, so it's fine!

10:34.570 --> 10:37.310
Dates are very nice things.

10:37.310 --> 10:38.930
I had fun, Touya.

10:38.930 --> 10:40.410
I'm glad to hear that.

10:40.410 --> 10:42.980
Feel free to come hang out 
whenever I'm not busy.

10:46.970 --> 10:49.330
You really are incredible.

10:49.330 --> 10:50.690
How so?

10:50.690 --> 10:53.610
Everyone goes about their life 
with a smile in this country.

10:53.610 --> 10:55.400
You're a good monarch.

10:55.400 --> 10:56.660
Am I?

10:56.660 --> 10:58.300
I'm not so confident.

10:58.750 --> 11:00.990
What do you have to worry about?

11:00.990 --> 11:03.760
You have us with you, don't you?

11:05.100 --> 11:09.510
So you should be more confident 
and do what you want to do.

11:10.310 --> 11:12.020
That's reassuring to hear.

11:12.020 --> 11:13.900
I guess I'm just invincible?

11:15.790 --> 11:21.260
<i>At first, I was okay with a nation in 
name only that was nothing but my family.</i>

11:22.100 --> 11:24.050
Touya? What's the matter?

11:24.050 --> 11:26.120
Oh, it's nothing.

11:28.550 --> 11:33.530
<i>I need to do what I can so the people 
of this nation can live in happiness, too.</i>

11:33.530 --> 11:35.590
<i>Master, can you hear me?</i>

11:35.590 --> 11:36.590
<i>Kohaku?</i>

11:37.890 --> 11:40.040
<i>Master, this is Flora.</i>

11:40.040 --> 11:41.930
<i>What is it? Did something happen?</i>

11:41.930 --> 11:45.100
<i>I've finished extracting the Ether Liquid.</i>

11:46.370 --> 11:47.770
It's finished?!

12:07.830 --> 12:10.510
It's really impressive to see 
up here on the ground.

12:10.510 --> 12:12.060
Will it really move?

12:12.060 --> 12:13.960
That's what we're about to find out.

12:14.320 --> 12:16.710
<i>Is Yae ready on her end, Kougyoku?</i>

12:16.710 --> 12:18.550
She says she's ready whenever you are.

12:18.550 --> 12:19.730
All right.

12:19.730 --> 12:22.110
Chevalier, activate!

12:31.670 --> 12:33.030
It moved!

12:53.890 --> 12:56.040
Good work. How was it?

12:56.440 --> 12:59.480
It was easier to pilot than I expected.

12:59.480 --> 13:02.770
It wasn't any different 
from the Frame Units.

13:02.770 --> 13:04.060
I see.

13:04.060 --> 13:05.400
But Touya...

13:06.300 --> 13:08.740
Why weren't you the first to pilot it?

13:08.740 --> 13:12.450
You were really looking forward to 
piloting a Frame Gear, right?

13:12.450 --> 13:15.560
That's because Yae has 
the lowest magic capacity.

13:15.560 --> 13:17.600
I figured if Yae could freely pilot it,

13:17.600 --> 13:20.480
others would be able to pilot it, too.

13:20.480 --> 13:23.110
Of course, the next to pilot it will be...

13:23.110 --> 13:24.240
Huh?

13:27.200 --> 13:29.220
What?! Who's in there?!

13:29.220 --> 13:31.790
I'm sorry! My sister went in on her own!

13:31.790 --> 13:33.090
No way!

13:33.090 --> 13:36.210
I was dead set on being 
the next one to pilot it!

13:36.750 --> 13:38.250
Yahoo!

13:38.250 --> 13:41.750
So excited! So excited!

13:40.050 --> 13:41.750
My turn...

13:42.950 --> 13:45.590
This is your anti-Phrase weapon.

13:46.030 --> 13:48.260
Yeah, it looks well-made.

13:48.730 --> 13:50.180
Thanks, Rosetta.

13:50.180 --> 13:54.580
Still, making weapons 
out of Phrase crystals?

13:54.580 --> 13:57.890
You sure come up with 
incredible ideas, Master.

13:58.440 --> 14:02.410
The Phrase's bodies increase in strength 
as more mana pours into them.

14:02.410 --> 14:06.240
I figured we could make an 
incredible weapon out of them,

14:06.890 --> 14:10.370
so I put the fragments of the 
defeated Phrase into Storage.

14:11.580 --> 14:14.680
I made several additional swords, as well.

14:14.680 --> 14:17.540
I also made you several crystal bullets.

14:17.540 --> 14:18.880
Thanks.

14:19.250 --> 14:21.300
How are the Frame Gears coming along?

14:21.300 --> 14:23.850
Mass production is underway.

14:23.850 --> 14:26.440
Though we're getting low on Orichalcum,

14:26.440 --> 14:28.430
so I'll need you to replenish that.

14:29.140 --> 14:30.960
Orichalcum, huh?

14:33.350 --> 14:35.680
<i>How do we acquire that?</i>

14:35.680 --> 14:36.410
Touya!

14:36.410 --> 14:37.680
Touya!

14:38.910 --> 14:40.650
Yumina, Lu.

14:40.650 --> 14:44.400
Good grief, what are you 
ignoring your wives to do now?

14:44.400 --> 14:46.990
You're not my wives yet.

14:46.990 --> 14:49.780
We're already your wives in our minds.

14:49.780 --> 14:53.360
We're birds of a feather, entwined branches.

14:53.360 --> 14:56.490
Wait... Maybe it's slightly 
different in our case?

14:56.490 --> 14:59.250
Well, that would be a lot 
of feathers and branches.

14:59.250 --> 15:02.130
So why do you have such a 
thoughtful look on your face?

15:02.470 --> 15:06.840
I need to acquire some 
Orichalcum for the Frame Gears,

15:06.840 --> 15:09.850
but I'm not sure where to get it.

15:09.850 --> 15:13.690
I imagine they would be 
selling some at a mineral shop,

15:13.690 --> 15:15.980
but they probably wouldn't 
have enough, right?

15:15.980 --> 15:18.140
It is a rare mineral.

15:18.140 --> 15:20.100
It fetches a rather high price, too.

15:20.560 --> 15:24.370
And I want to save money, 
considering our future.

15:24.370 --> 15:27.070
We still have plenty of mythril left over...

15:27.690 --> 15:30.430
Are Orichalcum Golems a thing?

15:31.110 --> 15:33.320
You know, like Mythril Golems.

15:33.320 --> 15:35.450
An Orichalcum Golem?

15:35.450 --> 15:36.960
I've never heard of one.

15:36.960 --> 15:38.410
Neither have I.

15:38.760 --> 15:40.790
I guess I'll try searching.

15:40.790 --> 15:43.380
Search: Orichalcum Golem.

15:43.380 --> 15:45.040
Commencing Search.

15:45.420 --> 15:47.660
Complete. Displaying now.

15:48.960 --> 15:50.340
There's quite a few.

15:50.910 --> 15:52.750
Well, guess I'll go hunt some down.

15:52.750 --> 15:55.210
Are you planning to leave us alone again?

15:55.210 --> 15:59.260
Th-That's not my intention, 
but it's my first time going there,

15:59.260 --> 16:01.530
so I was planning to use Fly to fly there.

16:01.530 --> 16:02.730
You want to come with me?

16:03.160 --> 16:04.730
Fly, you say?

16:04.730 --> 16:08.110
Flying is a little scary.

16:08.680 --> 16:10.780
That's what I figured.

16:15.740 --> 16:18.610
<i>The sky above Lestia, huh?</i>

16:18.610 --> 16:20.250
<i>Just a little farther.</i>

16:22.410 --> 16:23.610
Smoke?

16:23.610 --> 16:24.760
Long Sense.

16:25.240 --> 16:26.450
A fire?

16:27.500 --> 16:28.840
Phrase?!

16:34.860 --> 16:35.890
Stand your ground!

16:39.190 --> 16:42.390
Buy more time for the townsfolk to escape!

16:42.390 --> 16:44.940
Do not yield a single step!

16:47.200 --> 16:48.860
It's so tough!

17:05.850 --> 17:09.720
Yeah, I thought this blade 
would be able to cut Phrase, too.

17:11.010 --> 17:12.250
<i>Inferior Phrase?</i>

17:12.250 --> 17:15.970
<i>Then if I can get their cores with Apport 
and break them, that should end it.</i>

17:16.730 --> 17:19.810
Time to see just how well this thing can cut.

17:19.810 --> 17:21.570
Wh-Who are you?

17:21.570 --> 17:23.910
Leave this to me and 
evacuate the residents.

17:23.910 --> 17:25.160
We'll talk later.

17:25.160 --> 17:26.620
U-Understood.

17:26.620 --> 17:27.800
I'll leave it to you.

17:27.800 --> 17:30.010
Okay, I'm your opponent now.

17:30.010 --> 17:31.630
Accel Boost!

17:42.890 --> 17:44.220
We're saved.

17:45.620 --> 17:46.830
Thank goodness.

17:48.260 --> 17:50.000
Are you all right?

17:50.000 --> 17:52.660
I'm fine. How was the damage on your end?

17:53.100 --> 17:53.800
Huh?

17:53.800 --> 17:56.690
O-Oh, many were injured,

17:56.690 --> 17:58.640
but fortunately, there were no casualties.

17:58.640 --> 17:59.790
That's good.

17:59.790 --> 18:02.250
Then I'll heal the injured with my magic.

18:02.250 --> 18:02.870
Huh?

18:03.290 --> 18:04.810
Come Forth, Light.

18:05.560 --> 18:08.680
Impartial Healing, Area Heal.

18:15.100 --> 18:17.210
Just who are you?

18:17.810 --> 18:19.850
I'm Mochizuki Touya.

18:19.850 --> 18:22.100
I just happened to be passing by.

18:22.100 --> 18:22.910
And you?

18:23.230 --> 18:29.230
I-I am the first princess of the Knight 
Kingdom of Lestia, Hildegard Minas Lestia.

18:29.230 --> 18:31.420
You have my gratitude for your aid.

18:31.870 --> 18:33.650
<i>A princess?</i>

18:33.650 --> 18:37.300
<i>If I recall, Lestia is a big 
nation ruled by a knight king.</i>

18:37.300 --> 18:40.240
My apologies. I didn't know 
you were a princess of Lestia.

18:40.240 --> 18:44.220
I am Mochizuki Touya, 
Grand Duke of the Brunhild Duchy.

18:44.220 --> 18:45.860
Brunhild?

18:45.860 --> 18:47.820
I've heard of you.

18:47.820 --> 18:50.620
They say you're the young monarch 
who rose up from an adventurer,

18:50.620 --> 18:53.490
and the mediator who's been 
resolving problems in many nations.

18:53.490 --> 18:55.550
No, no, I'm not that great.

18:55.550 --> 18:57.190
<i>That's how people have been 
talking about me?</i>

18:57.190 --> 18:59.570
<i>I know I've been solving 
national problems, but still...</i>

18:59.570 --> 19:04.870
So you're skilled with a sword, 
in addition to being clever.

19:04.870 --> 19:07.820
I'm surprised you could basically defeat 
that monster in a single blow

19:07.820 --> 19:10.260
when we were no match for it together.

19:10.580 --> 19:12.670
This monster is called a Phrase.

19:12.670 --> 19:16.210
You can't defeat it without 
destroying the core inside its body.

19:16.210 --> 19:17.550
Phrase...

19:18.040 --> 19:19.560
From what I could see,

19:19.560 --> 19:22.100
you're pretty good with a sword, too.

19:22.100 --> 19:25.430
Your opponent this time was 
just a bad match, that's all.

19:25.430 --> 19:26.340
Yes.

19:26.700 --> 19:28.390
Oh, also...

19:30.790 --> 19:34.680
Do you mind if I take the fragments 
of these Phrase I defeated?

19:34.680 --> 19:35.360
Huh?

19:35.360 --> 19:36.830
Oh, yes.

19:36.830 --> 19:40.790
You defeated them, so that's not an issue.

19:40.790 --> 19:42.320
Am I right that your sword...

19:42.320 --> 19:44.570
was made from the Phrase?

19:44.570 --> 19:46.260
That's right.

19:46.260 --> 19:49.200
Though you can't create one 
without some unique processing.

19:49.200 --> 19:50.750
I see.

19:55.680 --> 19:57.110
Uh...

19:58.130 --> 19:59.980
M-My apologies.

19:59.980 --> 20:05.140
As a knight, I thought it would be nice 
to wield a sword like that one day.

20:05.510 --> 20:07.350
<i>She must want it pretty bad.</i>

20:08.390 --> 20:11.980
<i>I suppose it would be a good idea to 
build good relations with Lestia now.</i>

20:12.960 --> 20:14.180
Storage.

20:18.630 --> 20:19.800
I'll give you this one.

20:19.800 --> 20:22.200
If you'd like, you can have 
some for the royal family, too.

20:23.080 --> 20:24.750
A-Are you sure?

20:26.660 --> 20:29.080
Yeah. It's to commemorate our meeting.

20:32.960 --> 20:34.180
Something wrong?

20:34.180 --> 20:37.030
No! I-I-It's nothing!

20:37.030 --> 20:38.820
Thank you very much!

20:39.660 --> 20:41.160
I'll gladly accept it!

20:41.760 --> 20:44.500
Well, pardon me, but I'll be going now.

20:44.500 --> 20:46.050
I hope we meet again.

20:46.050 --> 20:47.050
Yes!

20:47.050 --> 20:49.600
Thank you so much for the lovely present!

20:53.260 --> 20:55.950
Yay! Yay!

21:03.740 --> 21:04.900
Storage.

21:07.030 --> 21:09.400
There, mission complete.

21:10.700 --> 21:15.770
Though that Orichalcum Golem was more 
golden and sparkly than I expected.

21:21.140 --> 21:22.200
A deer?

21:54.710 --> 21:55.940
Come Forth, Light!

21:55.940 --> 21:58.480
The Goddess's Healing, Mega Heal!

22:07.630 --> 22:09.050
Are you coming to?

22:12.340 --> 22:13.290
Hey!

22:13.290 --> 22:14.510
Are you okay?!

22:14.510 --> 22:15.440
Hey!

22:30.770 --> 22:33.790
Every day is bittersweet

22:33.790 --> 22:36.200
(Bubbly bubbly)

22:36.200 --> 22:41.670
I might still blush when 
your eyes are close up

22:42.860 --> 22:47.280
Our love affair goes around with 
the 1, 2, 3 beat of I, My, Me, Mine

22:47.280 --> 22:50.150
But "Look solely at me"

22:50.520 --> 22:56.280
Is something I can't say; 
I want you to notice my jealousy

22:57.560 --> 23:00.210
My hero glimpsed through a lens

23:00.210 --> 23:04.010
I want you to take everything, 
even your flawed kindness

23:04.010 --> 23:06.720
And fill me up with goodness even more

23:06.720 --> 23:09.390
(even more)

23:09.390 --> 23:12.230
Until I burst

23:12.230 --> 23:17.270
My heart races and aches deep 
within because I love you

23:17.270 --> 23:22.720
My love is rapidly rising, 
but, but, but, but

23:22.720 --> 23:26.510
I can't help that we're in another world

23:26.510 --> 23:31.600
Let's sing about this joyous occasion 
illuminated by the brilliant sun!

23:31.600 --> 23:33.630
"Together forever!"

23:33.630 --> 23:37.920
I may not be much, but I want you 
to hug me from time to time,

23:37.920 --> 23:39.520
And if you're far away, that's okey-dokey

23:39.520 --> 23:42.010
We'll live happily ever after!
